{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>If it be so, those at peace with me</b> — from the light binyan, even though 'those at peace with me' is not found in the light binyan, but only in the heavy. And some say: he who was at peace with me." "And the meaning of <b>and I stripped my pursuers empty</b>: And how would I do evil to those at peace with me, when I strip the foes and haters who hate me without cause — and this is the meaning of <b>empty</b> — after the manner of: 'and I anointed my king' [etc.]. And Rabbi Moses said: the vav is like 'empty,' as in 'and your servants came to buy food.' And some say: <b>and I stripped</b> — after the manner of 'and they stripped Egypt,' but this is far-fetched."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:01.005006377Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}